"""Original fictional social-enterprise launch practicum."""


def build(c, m):
    return c(83, 'Social Enterprise Launch Practicum', 'Social Enterprise\nLaunch\nPracticum',
        'Integrate mission, market, operations, finance, governance and impact into a conditional fictional launch proposal with explicit review and authority gates.', [
        m('Build a coherent fictional enterprise proposal', 'Connect an invented problem and offer to evidence, resources and a bounded decision.', [
            'A launch proposal should explain a decision, not merely assemble attractive sections. Begin with the invented social concern, the intended group, the offer and the proposed change. Identify who uses, pays and benefits, then show how resources and activities connect those roles. Foundation enterprise learning brings opportunity, resources and action together under support. Keep the proposal conditional: a classroom submission is a plan for reasoning, not an operating enterprise or a demonstration of professional competence. Do not register a venture, solicit money or recruit participants through this exercise. [S62]',
            'Use a short claim record for the most important statements. Mark each as a supplied fictional observation, a calculation, an external contextual finding or an assumption. Include source and relevant date so a publication year is not confused with fieldwork. A sector review of food and nutrition enterprises can inform questions about models and mission, while its selection and appraisal limits prevent a guaranteed survival claim for the invented venture. State the particular question the evidence helps frame, rather than adding a citation to make an unsupported forecast look certain. [R72]',
            'Make the offer and operating requirements agree. If the fictional market note promises same-day repair, the capacity, staffing and supply sequence must support that promise. Separate an expression of interest from a confirmed order and a revenue forecast from actual receipts. General business planning helps structure those questions, but does not validate local legal or tax assumptions. Identify any service-quality or access condition the proposal has not resolved and name the qualified role that would need to verify it before a real commitment could occur. [S61]',
            'Compare at least two feasible options under common headings rather than selecting the most exciting presentation. Include mission, practical access, demand evidence, delivery capacity, cost, cash timing, control and uncertainty. State what would change the preferred choice. Impact guidance supports using evidence for decisions and learning, so the proposal should make its assumptions examinable. The final output is an original fictional enterprise note, with a clear next decision and bounded claims. It should not imply that a neat plan proves trading demand, beneficiary improvement or readiness to launch a real service. [S64]'],
            'An invented repair-and-learning proposal promises same-day service, forecasts sales from favourable comments and cites a sector review as proof of survival. Staffing and the source of subsidy are unspecified.',
            'Write a one-paragraph proposal and four claim-record entries. Compare two options and identify an assumption that could reverse the preferred choice.',
            'Connect the promise to evidence and resources. Comments, contextual studies and forecasts are different claim types; unverified capacity and subsidy remain decision limits.', ['S62', 'R72', 'S61', 'S64'], [
                ('A proposal should connect its parts to a decision.', 'Which fictional proposal is coherent?', 'Mission, offer, evidence and resources leading to a bounded next decision.', ['A set of slogans with no delivery requirements.', 'A guarantee of survival from a citation.', 'A real launch instruction issued by coursework.'], 'The sections should support an examinable decision.'),
                ('Claim types should remain distinguishable.', 'How should the invented claim record classify a sales forecast?', 'An assumption-based projection, distinct from actual receipts.', ['A verified historical transaction.', 'A controlled social-outcome result.', 'An automatic funding commitment.'], 'A projection describes expectations under assumptions.'),
                ('Contextual research does not guarantee survival.', 'What is wrong with the fictional sector-review claim?', 'The review does not establish universal survival for this venture.', ['Research can never inform a question.', 'Only publication date matters.', 'Every case report is a randomised trial.'], 'The design and sector limits must accompany transfer to a new proposal.'),
                ('Promises must match operating capacity.', 'What must support the fictional same-day offer?', 'A feasible staffing and supply sequence with stated limits.', ['Only an attractive cover page.', 'An assumption that goodwill creates capacity.', 'No review of quality.'], 'The promise depends on resources and an operating process.'),
                ('Options should identify what could change the choice.', 'Which addition strengthens the fictional recommendation?', 'A condition that would justify reconsidering the preferred option.', ['A claim of certainty regardless of evidence.', 'Removal of contrary records.', 'An invented empirical success rate.'], 'A conditional choice remains open to evidence.')]),
        m('Plan readiness responsibilities and a limited test', 'Identify dependencies and authority gates before a fictional pilot or expansion.', [
            'Readiness means that the requirements for a particular next step have been checked, rather than that enthusiasm is high. For the invented venture, map a sequence from an enquiry to an agreed service, delivery, payment and a response to a concern. Identify the responsible role, capacity and information needed at each step. General business planning supports attention to operations and resources. A task completed on paper does not prove that a real institution has authority, staff or permits. Keep legal, employment, safeguarding and finance requirements explicitly subject to qualified local verification. [S61]',
            'Include finance and governance in the same readiness review. A positive contribution can coexist with an early cash shortfall, while external finance may change member control or the mission promise. The cooperative identity provides questions about democratic accountability and autonomy, not a licence to accept deposits or an assurance of returns. In the fictional plan, record who can approve a commitment and what information must be available before that approval. Do not let a simulated member vote stand in for registered legal arrangements or appropriate advice about real obligations. [S63]',
            'A limited learning test should use invented records and a defined question. Specify what would be observed, the resources needed and a condition for modifying or pausing. A startup assessment study may help question the relationship between a tool and its evidence, but its artificial tests do not establish the impact of a new venture. Therefore do not treat the existence of a prototype or a completed scoring sheet as permission to expand. Record whether the fictional test examines clarity, process, capacity or a proposed outcome, and preserve the original question. [R71]',
            'Partnership dependencies also need owners and a response if an assumption fails. If an invented supplier cannot meet a delivery schedule, the team may need to change the offer rather than hide the delay. Qualitative partnership evidence illustrates contextual tensions, not a universal contract recipe. The practicum should identify the dependency, a responsible review role and the effect on mission and feasibility. A useful readiness note can recommend a pause pending evidence. It must not expose real confidential records, sign an agreement or move a fictional pilot into actual public service without verified authority. [R74]'],
            'An invented launch checklist marks every requirement ready because slides are complete. The buyer pays late, a supplier is unconfirmed and an external funder controls member decisions. The team plans immediate expansion.',
            'Map four readiness gates with owners and evidence. Define a limited fictional test and a condition for pausing or modifying the plan.',
            'Teaching completion is not operating readiness. Cash timing, supply, control and authority need explicit evidence; a bounded simulation can inform a further decision.', ['S61', 'S63', 'R71', 'R74'], [
                ('Readiness is specific to an evidenced next step.', 'What does a completed fictional slide deck fail to prove?', 'Operational authority, resources and service readiness.', ['That a learning artifact exists.', 'That a proposal can be reviewed.', 'That further checks can be named.'], 'A teaching artifact and an operating arrangement are different things.'),
                ('Cash and control belong in readiness.', 'Which fictional issues must be reviewed before a commitment?', 'Late receipts and external control of member decisions.', ['Only whether the logo looks professional.', 'Only projected annual sales.', 'Neither because the mission is social.'], 'Timing and governance can change feasibility and mission.'),
                ('A test should state its question and limit.', 'Which fictional pilot description is adequate?', 'A defined observation, required resources and a modify/pause condition.', ['Expansion guaranteed before observing anything.', 'No record of the original question.', 'A score labelled automatic impact proof.'], 'A learning test needs a clear decision boundary.'),
                ('Partner dependencies need a response.', 'An invented supplier is unconfirmed. What should the plan show?', 'A responsible verification role and effect on the service promise.', ['A guarantee of delivery anyway.', 'Deletion of the dependency.', 'A learner signing a real agreement.'], 'A dependency should remain visible until verified.'),
                ('Cooperative identity is not a regulated-service permission.', 'What does the fictional cooperative note not authorise?', 'Taking real deposits or guaranteeing investor returns.', ['Discussion of member control.', 'A question about accountability.', 'An invented comparison of terms.'], 'Identity principles do not confer financial-service authority.')]),
        m('Present a launch decision and learning review', 'Recommend continue, modify or pause with honest results and recognition boundaries.', [
            'The final practicum should state a clear conditional decision: continue the fictional design, modify a specified part or pause until a requirement is resolved. Explain the reason using mission, evidence and feasibility together. Identify the responsible role and the observation that would justify a later decision. Supported entrepreneurship learning includes reflection on experience as well as initiative. Do not reward an unrealistic launch promise merely because it sounds decisive. A reasoned pause can demonstrate good judgement when capacity, access, cash or authority remains unresolved in the supplied case. [S62]',
            'Use a small review plan with a question, measure, denominator, period and source. Separate process completion from the outcome the venture intends to support, and include missing or adverse observations. Proportionate impact guidance encourages learning rather than a collection of favourable counts. If the fictional test changes, retain the original version, reason and decision owner. A report should distinguish a planned action, an accepted recommendation, a completed change and a result that has actually been examined. Downloads, attendance and sales are not interchangeable with mission achievement. [S64]',
            'Keep research transfer honest in the presentation. The Slovenian study concerns measurement adoption using a 2021 survey and historical accounts, although it was published in 2026. Its associations do not establish which financing source will deliver the best social outcome in another setting. A practical tool or an attractive dashboard can structure discussion without validating the underlying claim. State the evidence limit in plain language and identify what would still need checking before a real decision. Do not manufacture confidence by substituting a journal quartile for the actual study design and outcome. [R73]',
            'Submit the fictional proposal, claim record, options comparison, cost and cash notes, readiness gates and learning review together. Explain any unresolved mission tension and how a relevant affected perspective would be heard through an appropriate process. Completion is educational evidence, not permission to trade or provide finance. Recognition also has separate conditions: a course badge requires a verified course CBT pass, while a school certificate requires every approved course, the final mixed ParaLearn exam, human written marking, independent moderation and authorised signatures. Reading or presenting the materials alone satisfies neither credential condition. [S62]'],
            'An invented team calls downloads proof of impact and a 2026 survey publication proof of current local financing effects. It hides a cash shortfall and promises school certificates after the presentation.',
            'Present a conditional decision with three reasons and a review measure. Correct the date, impact and credential claims, and identify a finding that would change the decision.',
            'State the shortfall and limits; downloads do not establish impact, publication is not fieldwork and the presentation cannot replace verified course passes or the moderated school exam.', ['S62', 'S64', 'R73'], [
                ('A reasoned pause can demonstrate sound judgement.', 'Which fictional launch recommendation is defensible with unresolved cash and capacity?', 'Pause or modify pending specified authorised checks.', ['Launch regardless because confidence is important.', 'Hide the shortfall.', 'Claim every requirement is already met.'], 'The decision should reflect the actual evidence and dependencies.'),
                ('Review measures should match the question.', 'What should accompany a fictional completion count?', 'Definition, denominator, period, source and missing outcomes.', ['Only a success headline.', 'An assumed causal effect.', 'Deletion of incomplete cases.'], 'A count needs context before it can inform learning.'),
                ('Publication date differs from data period.', 'The measurement study was published in 2026 using a 2021 survey. What is accurate?', 'State both dates and the contextual limits.', ['Call it current local 2026 fieldwork.', 'Ignore the survey period.', 'Treat the date as proof of causal strength.'], 'Publication timing does not change when or where observations were made.'),
                ('Recognition requires verified assessment conditions.', 'What is required beyond reading the fictional practicum materials for a course badge?', 'An approved course and a verified ParaLearn course CBT pass.', ['Only downloads.', 'Only a presentation attendance mark.', 'A self-declared completion statement.'], 'Learning-resource access does not itself satisfy the badge condition.'),
                ('School certification has a separate integrated assessment gate.', 'Which statement fits the proposed SEE certificate pathway?', 'All approved courses plus the moderated mixed ParaLearn exam and authorised signatures.', ['A certificate after viewing slides alone.', 'Automatic certification from an offline review fixture.', 'No human review of essays is needed.'], 'School certification requires completion, verified assessment and authorised signatories.')])])
